    "description": "Write code through a disciplined, BDD-framed Test-Driven Development loop: build a behavior test list, then drive each behavior through red-green-refactor with an enforced observed-failure gate. Use when the user wants to implement, build, or write code test-first, \"do TDD\", follow \"red-green-refactor\", drive code from tests, or grow a feature behavior-by-behavior with tests leading. This skill writes and changes code; it does not produce a test plan document (use test-planning), review or audit existing code (use code-review), restructure existing code outside a TDD loop (use refactor), specify what a feature should do (use plan-a-feature), or find the root cause of a bug (use investigate).\n",
